<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Worms ruin baptisms in Irish town.</title>
<headline>Worms ruin baptisms in Irish town.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Priests in the western Irish town of Galway are refusing to use tap water for baptisms because it is teeming with worms.</p>
<p>Father Christy O'Byrne told the Examiner newspaper the water supply was infested with wriggling white creatures and was brown and cloudy.</p>
<p>Galway residents have made a video of the infestation, which they plan to send to the Health Ministry in protest, the newspaper said.</p>
